vtund server: say who was denied and why.

Stock 3.0.2 logs a failed login only as "Denied connection from IP:PORT", so a
wrong password, an unknown session and a refused second login look the same
and the device cannot be identified. Log the session name the client sent
(sanitised to printable ASCII) and the reason:

  Denied connection from 1.2.3.4:5678: session 02BE0C000001: wrong password
  Denied connection from 1.2.3.4:5678: session 02BE0C0000FF: unknown session
  Denied connection from 1.2.3.4:5678: session 02BE0C000005: already connected (multi no) or lock error
  Denied connection from 1.2.3.4:5678: no session name received

The wire protocol is unchanged: the client still gets a bare "ERR".

